  zk:{title:'Verifying defined statements',eyebrow:'ZERO KNOWLEDGE',summary:'Zero-knowledge proofs can verify a defined statement while separating public inputs from private witnesses. Public Xythum materials present this as a core research direction.',roles:['Prove a defined condition','Limit disclosure of private witnesses','Support settlement checks without revealing every input'],limits:['Proof strength follows from the statement, circuit, public inputs, and input validation.','Network and timing privacy are addressed by complementary layers.','Published circuit revisions will make implementation review reproducible.'],questions:['What exact statement is proved?','Which inputs are public?','Who audits and versions the circuit?']},
  tee:{title:'Protected execution environments',eyebrow:'TEE',summary:'The original materials discuss trusted execution environments as a protected computation layer supported by hardware attestation and versioned enclave code.',roles:['Isolate selected computation','Attest to an expected execution environment','Reduce host visibility into protected workloads'],limits:['Hardware, attestation, firmware, code, and side-channel controls shape the protection model.','TEEs contribute a focused layer within a broader trust architecture.','Resilience planning can define updates and recovery.'],questions:['Which attestation policy is accepted?','How are enclave updates governed?','What happens after a vendor or firmware compromise?']},
  'cross-chain':{title:'Cross-chain execution boundaries',eyebrow:'CROSS-CHAIN',summary:'The original Xythum vision connects private processing with chain-specific execution. Source observation, finality, authorization, replay protection, and recovery rules make that connection precise.',roles:['Observe a source-chain condition','Coordinate authorization between environments','Submit a destination-chain operation'],limits:['Atomicity and settlement behavior follow the specified execution model.','Each chain contributes its own finality and recovery model.','Liquidity and recovery policies complete the operational design.'],questions:['How many source confirmations are required?','How are duplicate messages rejected?','What is the refund path after destination failure?']},
